text.paragraph:
Warnings and Precautions (
                              5.8
                           )                                                            2/2026

Advise patients that teriflunomide may stay in the blood for up to 2 years after the last dose and that an accelerated elimination procedure may be used if needed [see Warnings and Precautions (
                        5.3
                        )
                     ].

Inform patients that they may be more likely to get infections when taking teriflunomide tablets and that they should contact their physician if they develop symptoms of infection, particularly in case of fever [see Warnings and Precautions (
                        5.4
                        )
                     ].
